SOAPBOX: Had a great time in the contest after raising my EFHW from 17' to 65'! Almost doubled my score from last year. Had fun working on scheduling my 24 hours for the classic overlay. 10 and 15 proved great again with lots of contacts. 40 is always very difficult to work because of cramming everyone into roughly 75khz of space. Still was able to have a great time in the contest!
SOAPBOX: Unfortunately my trusty Yaesu 767GX decided to die on me about 3 hours into the contest. Good thing I had my spare Yaesu 891 (my backup pota rig) ready to go just in case. Just shows how important it is to have backups and spares.
